WEBVTT

00:00:06.949 --> 00:00:10.913
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:12.755 --> 00:00:14.558
Mary! No!

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:18.864
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.802
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:21.915 --> 00:00:23.237
Jess excuse us.

00:00:25.798 --> 00:00:27.191
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:27.824 --> 00:00:28.541
For good.

00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:29.484
I can't do this alone.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.665
Now you're taking off the middle of the
night to spend the week-End with them.

00:00:32.666 --> 00:00:35.166
Hey, everything's gonna be OK.

00:00:35.209 --> 00:00:36.479
I promise.

00:00:38.354 --> 00:00:39.768
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.716
Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:00:41.771 --> 00:00:44.855
You have a responsability.
To dad and his cruisade.

00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:48.400
Even if you do find the thing
that killed her, mom's gone

00:00:48.796 --> 00:00:50.966
And she isn't coming back.

00:00:51.503 --> 00:00:53.632
Don't talk about her like that.

00:00:54.778 --> 00:00:55.735
Dad's gone.

00:00:55.796 --> 00:00:57.439
I've got his journal.
He left me a message.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.754
It's coordinates he
left us. It's weird, man.

00:00:59.837 --> 00:01:00.431
Hey, Dean,

00:01:00.541 --> 00:01:01.495
What I said earlier,

00:01:01.573 --> 00:01:02.919
I'm sorry.

00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:04.922
No chick-Flick moments.

00:01:06.694 --> 00:01:07.727
Yes.

00:01:17.085 --> 00:01:18.149
No!

00:01:29.228 --> 00:01:31.762
We got work to do.

00:02:10.209 --> 00:02:11.629
Dude, you're cheating.

00:02:11.956 --> 00:02:14.126
No, you just suck.

00:02:20.391 --> 00:02:23.433
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:27.434
We're fine, keeping safe, so
don't worry. Talk to you tomorrow.

00:02:36.761 --> 00:02:39.150
Hey, where you going?
My moment of victory.

00:02:39.272 --> 00:02:40.815
Nature calls.

00:03:23.039 --> 00:03:24.022
Brad?

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.316
Gary, what's going on?

00:04:45.235 --> 00:04:47.896
I am, um...

00:04:48.598 --> 00:04:54.030
You always said roses were
lame, so, I brought you, uh...

00:05:08.897 --> 00:05:10.316
Jess...

00:05:11.376 --> 00:05:12.658
Oh, god.

00:05:17.359 --> 00:05:19.024
I should have protected you.

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:22.072
I should have told you the truth.

00:05:38.724 --> 00:05:40.103
You okay?

00:05:40.512 --> 00:05:41.836
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:05:42.723 --> 00:05:44.115
Another nightmare?

00:05:49.983 --> 00:05:51.744
Want to drive for a while?

00:05:54.246 --> 00:05:57.440
In your whole life, you
never once asked me that.

00:05:57.898 --> 00:06:00.333
Just thought you might
want to. Never mind.

00:06:01.059 --> 00:06:02.154
Look, man,

00:06:02.707 --> 00:06:05.038
You're worried about
me. I get it, and ...

00:06:05.226 --> 00:06:08.934
Thank you, but I'm perfectly okay.

00:06:12.006 --> 00:06:14.415
All right. Where are we?

00:06:14.822 --> 00:06:17.497
We are just outside of Grand Junction.

00:06:21.666 --> 00:06:25.014
You know what? Maybe we shouldn't
have left Stanford so soon.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.082
Sam, we dug around there for a
week. We came up with nothing.

00:06:29.446 --> 00:06:33.201
If you want to find the thing that
killed Jessica... Got to find dad first.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.255
Dad disappearing, and this thing
showing up again after 20 years?

00:06:38.494 --> 00:06:40.340
It's no coincidence.

00:06:40.778 --> 00:06:44.157
Dad will have answers. He'll
know what to do. It's weird, man.

00:06:44.517 --> 00:06:47.943
These coordinates he left
us, this Black Water Ridge...

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.550
What about it? There's nothing there.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:53.621
It's just woods.

00:06:55.357 --> 00:06:58.158
Why is he sending us to
the middle of nowhere?

00:07:05.105 --> 00:07:07.405
So Black Water Ridge is pretty remote.

00:07:07.514 --> 00:07:10.881
It's cut off by these canyons
here --Rough terrain, dense forest,

00:07:10.882 --> 00:07:13.382
Abandoned silver and gold
mines all over the place...

00:07:13.507 --> 00:07:16.797
Dude, check out the size
of this friggin' bear.

00:07:19.332 --> 00:07:22.977
And a dozen or more
grizzlies in the area.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.767
It's no nature hike, that's for sure.

00:07:26.158 --> 00:07:29.897
You boys aren't planning to go out
near Black Water Ridge, by any chance?

00:07:30.163 --> 00:07:35.284
Oh, no, sir. We're environmental-Study majors
from U.C. Boulder-Just working on a paper.

00:07:35.378 --> 00:07:36.926
Recycle, man.

00:07:37.229 --> 00:07:38.371
Bull.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.954
You're friends with
that Hailey girl, right?

00:07:43.273 --> 00:07:43.899
Yes.

00:07:44.337 --> 00:07:45.901
Yes, we are.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.452
Ranger... Wilkinson.

00:07:49.285 --> 00:07:51.505
Well, I will tell you
exactly what I told her.

00:07:51.506 --> 00:07:56.906
Her brother filled out a backcountry permit saying
he wouldn't be back from Black Water until the 24th.

00:07:57.008 --> 00:07:59.558
So it's not exactly a
missing persons now, is it?

00:08:00.168 --> 00:08:03.250
Tell that girl to quit worrying.
I'm sure her brother's just fine.

00:08:03.407 --> 00:08:04.737
We will.

00:08:05.519 --> 00:08:07.569
Well, that Hailey girl's
quite a pistol, huh?

00:08:07.698 --> 00:08:09.404
That is putting it mildly.

00:08:09.565 --> 00:08:13.969
Actually, you know what would help is if I
could show her a copy of that backcountry permit.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.670
You know, so she could see
her brother's return date.

00:08:18.973 --> 00:08:21.445
Yeah. Heh heh.

00:08:21.586 --> 00:08:23.385
What, are you cruising
for a hookup or something?

00:08:23.447 --> 00:08:24.198
What do you mean?

00:08:24.312 --> 00:08:26.851
The coordinates point to Black Water
Ridge. So what are we waiting for?

00:08:26.852 --> 00:08:30.352
Let's just go find dad.
Why even talk to this girl?

00:08:30.461 --> 00:08:34.669
I don't know, maybe we should know what we're
walking into before we actually walk into it.

00:08:35.591 --> 00:08:36.530
What?

00:08:36.608 --> 00:08:39.910
Since when are you all "shoot
first, ask questions later" anyway?

00:08:40.176 --> 00:08:41.599
Since now.

00:08:43.524 --> 00:08:45.057
Oh, really?

00:08:48.563 --> 00:08:50.159
You must be Hailey Collins.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.302
I'm Dean, this is Sam. We're rangers with the
park service. Ranger Wilkinson sent us over.

00:08:54.303 --> 00:08:58.003
We wanted to ask you some
questions about your brother Tommy.

00:08:58.941 --> 00:09:00.756
Let me see some I.D.

00:09:03.659 --> 00:09:04.911
There you go.

00:09:11.701 --> 00:09:14.439
Come on in. Thanks.

00:09:15.644 --> 00:09:16.504
That yours?

00:09:16.739 --> 00:09:17.318
Yeah.

00:09:17.459 --> 00:09:18.570
Nice car.

00:09:23.491 --> 00:09:27.324
So, if Tommy's not due back for a
while, how do you know something's wrong?

00:09:27.563 --> 00:09:31.791
He checks in every day by cell. He
e-Mails photos, stupid little videos.

00:09:31.792 --> 00:09:34.292
But we haven't heard anything
in over three days now.

00:09:34.553 --> 00:09:36.493
Well, maybe he can't get cell reception.

00:09:36.795 --> 00:09:38.485
He's got a satellite phone, too.

00:09:38.876 --> 00:09:43.538
Could it be he's just having fun and
forgot to check in? He wouldn't do that.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.944
Our parents are gone. It's
just my two brothers and me.

00:09:47.945 --> 00:09:50.445
We all keep pretty
close tabs on each other.

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:53.870
Can I see the pictures
he sent you? Yeah.

00:09:54.762 --> 00:09:56.186
That's Tommy.

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:05.544
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:10:05.545 --> 00:10:09.545
We're fine, keeping safe, so don't
worry, okay? Talk to you tomorrow.

00:10:11.222 --> 00:10:14.464
We'll find your brother. We're heading
out to Black Water Ridge first thing.

00:10:14.465 --> 00:10:16.965
Then maybe I'll see you there.

00:10:17.918 --> 00:10:18.779
Look.

00:10:18.971 --> 00:10:20.817
I can't sit around here anymore,

00:10:21.052 --> 00:10:24.916
So I hired a guide. I'm heading out in the
morning, and I'm gonna find Tommy myself.

00:10:25.672 --> 00:10:27.951
I think I know how you feel.

00:10:30.084 --> 00:10:32.400
Hey, you mind forwarding these to me?

00:10:32.666 --> 00:10:33.636
Sure.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:41.909
So, Black Water Ridge doesn't get a
lot of traffic-Local campers mostly--

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:46.910
But, still, this past april, two hikers went
missing out there. They were never found.

00:10:46.977 --> 00:10:48.291
Any before that?

00:10:48.369 --> 00:10:48.980
Yeah.

00:10:49.027 --> 00:10:52.067
In 1982, eight different people
all vanished in the same year.

00:10:52.068 --> 00:10:54.268
Authorities said it
was a grizzly attack.

00:10:54.268 --> 00:10:59.468
And, again, in 1959, and
again, before that, in 1936.

00:10:59.577 --> 00:11:02.844
Every 23 years, just like clockwork.

00:11:03.285 --> 00:11:04.804
Okay, watch this.

00:11:05.033 --> 00:11:06.650
Here's the clincher.

00:11:07.538 --> 00:11:12.438
I downloaded that guy Tommy's
video to the laptop. Check this out.

00:11:13.778 --> 00:11:15.264
Do it again.

00:11:18.358 --> 00:11:23.699
That's three frames. It's a fraction of a
second. Whatever that thing is, it can move.

00:11:24.663 --> 00:11:26.999
I told you something weird was going on.

00:11:27.326 --> 00:11:29.972
Yeah. I got one more thing.

00:11:30.098 --> 00:11:35.030
In '59, one camper survived the
supposed grizzly attack, just a kid

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:37.317
Barely crawled out of the woods alive.

00:11:37.657 --> 00:11:39.065
Is there a name?

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:43.684
Look, ranger, I don't know why
you're asking me about this.

00:11:43.826 --> 00:11:46.673
It's public record. I was a kid.

00:11:46.876 --> 00:11:49.223
My parents got mauled by a... grizzly?

00:11:49.418 --> 00:11:50.904
That's what attacked them?

00:11:59.215 --> 00:12:01.452
The other people that
went missing that year,

00:12:01.656 --> 00:12:03.690
Those bear attacks, too?

00:12:05.928 --> 00:12:08.432
What about all the people
that went missing this year?

00:12:09.151 --> 00:12:10.747
Same thing?

00:12:12.848 --> 00:12:16.990
If we knew what we were dealing
with, we might be able to stop it.

00:12:18.919 --> 00:12:21.547
I seriously doubt that.

00:12:21.954 --> 00:12:23.033
Anyways,

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:26.689
I don't see the
difference it would make.

00:12:27.972 --> 00:12:29.849
You wouldn't believe me.

00:12:30.178 --> 00:12:32.399
Nobody ever did.

00:12:35.135 --> 00:12:36.622
Mr. Shaw

00:12:39.688 --> 00:12:41.565
What did you see?

00:12:46.146 --> 00:12:47.585
Nothing.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:52.404
It moved too fast to see.

00:12:52.451 --> 00:12:54.062
It hid too well.

00:12:54.176 --> 00:12:55.663
I heard it, though.

00:12:56.257 --> 00:12:58.228
A roar

00:12:59.981 --> 00:13:00.873
Like ...

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:04.526
No man or animal I ever heard.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:06.619
It came at night?

00:13:07.308 --> 00:13:09.185
Got inside your tent?

00:13:09.503 --> 00:13:11.991
It got inside our cabin.

00:13:12.789 --> 00:13:16.669
I was sleeping in front of
the fireplace when it came in.

00:13:17.315 --> 00:13:20.397
It didn't smash a
window or break the door,

00:13:21.043 --> 00:13:23.062
It unlocked it.

00:13:23.844 --> 00:13:27.693
Do you know of a bear that
could do something like that?

00:13:28.355 --> 00:13:32.188
I didn't even wake up until
I heard my parents screaming.

00:13:32.423 --> 00:13:33.565
It killed them?

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:35.974
Dragged them off into the night.

00:13:38.508 --> 00:13:43.843
Why it left me alive --I've been
asking myself that ever since.

00:13:48.275 --> 00:13:50.450
It did leave me this, though.

00:14:00.407 --> 00:14:04.271
There's something evil in those woods.

00:14:07.009 --> 00:14:09.403
It was some sort of a demon.

00:14:09.877 --> 00:14:13.401
Spirits and demons don't have to unlock
doors. They just go through the walls.

00:14:13.402 --> 00:14:16.402
So it's probably something
else -Something corporeal.

00:14:16.531 --> 00:14:17.626
"Corporeal"?

00:14:17.892 --> 00:14:19.144
Excuse me, professor.

00:14:19.289 --> 00:14:21.151
Shut up. So, what do you think?

00:14:21.667 --> 00:14:24.108
The claws, the speed that it moves.

00:14:24.436 --> 00:14:26.580
It could be a skinwalker,
maybe a black dog

00:14:26.734 --> 00:14:31.365
Whatever we're talking about, we're talking
about a creature, and it's corporeal,

00:14:31.506 --> 00:14:33.623
Which means we can kill it.

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:53.023
We cannot let that
Hailey girl go out there.

00:14:53.085 --> 00:14:56.843
Oh yeah, what are we gonna tell her she can't go
into the woods because of a big, scary monster?

00:14:56.844 --> 00:14:58.844
Yeah.

00:14:59.583 --> 00:15:00.929
Her brother's missing, Sam.

00:15:01.132 --> 00:15:02.837
She's not just gonna sit this out.

00:15:03.135 --> 00:15:07.333
No, we go with her, we protect her, and we keep
our eyes peeled for our fuzzy predator friend

00:15:07.427 --> 00:15:09.351
So finding dad's not enough?

00:15:11.749 --> 00:15:13.955
Now we got to babysit, too?

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:17.726
What?

00:15:19.024 --> 00:15:20.057
Nothing.

00:15:27.091 --> 00:15:30.193
I'll tell you again. I
don't think ben should come.

00:15:30.804 --> 00:15:32.008
Roy...

00:15:32.483 --> 00:15:37.239
Look, you're paying me good money to keep
everybody safe. I think Ben's safest at home.

00:15:47.503 --> 00:15:49.145
You guys got room for two more?

00:15:49.338 --> 00:15:51.012
You want to come with us?

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:51.998
Who are these guys?

00:15:52.045 --> 00:15:55.409
Apparently, this is all the
park service could muster up.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:56.775
You're rangers?

00:15:56.822 --> 00:15:57.666
That's right.

00:15:57.823 --> 00:16:00.874
And you're hiking out
in biker boots and jeans?

00:16:02.141 --> 00:16:04.801
Well, sweet heart, I don't do shorts.

00:16:06.767 --> 00:16:11.163
Oh, you think this is funny? It's dangerous
backcountry out there. Her brother might be hurt.

00:16:13.541 --> 00:16:16.091
Believe me, I know how
dangerous it can be.

00:16:16.652 --> 00:16:19.124
We just want to help them
find their brother. That's all.

00:17:17.554 --> 00:17:19.885
Roy, you said you did a little hunting.

00:17:20.156 --> 00:17:22.143
Yeah, more than a little.

00:17:24.052 --> 00:17:25.761
What kind of furry critters do you hunt?

00:17:25.918 --> 00:17:28.405
Mostly buck. Sometimes bear.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:33.443
Tell me, uh, Bambi or
Yogi ever hunt you back?

00:17:37.456 --> 00:17:39.678
What you doing, Roy?

00:17:45.674 --> 00:17:48.303
You should watch where
you're stepping... ranger.

00:17:52.199 --> 00:17:54.311
It's a bear trap.

00:18:00.423 --> 00:18:02.707
You didn't pack any provisions.

00:18:02.816 --> 00:18:04.646
You guys are carrying a duffel bag.

00:18:04.756 --> 00:18:07.822
You're not rangers, so
who the hell are you?

00:18:16.392 --> 00:18:18.316
Sam and I are brothers,

00:18:18.614 --> 00:18:20.241
And we're looking for our father.

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:21.876
He might be here. We don't know.

00:18:22.016 --> 00:18:24.989
I just figured that you and
me, we're in the same boat.

00:18:26.637 --> 00:18:30.282
Why didn't you just tell me that
from the start? I'm telling you now.

00:18:30.767 --> 00:18:33.850
Besides, it's probably the most
honest I've ever been with a woman...

00:18:34.397 --> 00:18:35.664
Ever.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:38.391
So, we okay?

00:18:42.381 --> 00:18:44.196
Yeah, okay.

00:18:44.717 --> 00:18:47.048
And what do you mean I
didn't pack provisions?

00:19:03.827 --> 00:19:05.282
This is it.

00:19:05.689 --> 00:19:06.893
Black Water Ridge.

00:19:06.956 --> 00:19:08.818
What coordinates are we at?

00:19:12.776 --> 00:19:14.987
35 and minus 111.

00:19:20.322 --> 00:19:21.323
You hear that?

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:22.543
Yeah.

00:19:24.149 --> 00:19:25.901
Not even crickets.

00:19:26.668 --> 00:19:28.561
I'm gonna go take a look around.

00:19:28.926 --> 00:19:31.194
You shouldn't go off by yourself.

00:19:31.304 --> 00:19:34.746
That's sweet. Don't worry about me.

00:19:42.836 --> 00:19:46.701
All right, everybody
stays together. Let's go.

00:19:55.379 --> 00:19:57.413
Hailey! Over here!

00:20:05.007 --> 00:20:06.337
Oh, my god.

00:20:06.728 --> 00:20:08.496
Looks like a grizzly.

00:20:25.107 --> 00:20:26.280
Tommy?

00:20:28.079 --> 00:20:29.174
Tommy!

00:20:29.644 --> 00:20:32.151
Tommy! Shh... Shh...

00:20:32.945 --> 00:20:33.899
Why?

00:20:34.337 --> 00:20:35.964
Something might still be out there.

00:20:36.845 --> 00:20:37.878
Sam.

00:20:45.439 --> 00:20:47.931
The bodies were dragged
from the campsite.

00:20:49.042 --> 00:20:52.140
But here, the tracks just vanish.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.158
It's weird.

00:20:56.317 --> 00:20:58.570
I tell you what.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.590
It's no skinwalker or black dog.

00:21:24.603 --> 00:21:26.981
Hey, he could still be alive.

00:21:30.876 --> 00:21:33.020
Help!

00:21:54.497 --> 00:21:57.329
It seemed like it was coming
from around here, didn't it?

00:22:03.306 --> 00:22:05.496
Everybody back to camp.

00:22:11.511 --> 00:22:13.075
Our packs!

00:22:13.717 --> 00:22:16.752
So much for my GPS
and my satellite phone.

00:22:16.866 --> 00:22:18.227
What the hell's going on?

00:22:18.321 --> 00:22:19.432
It's smart.

00:22:19.510 --> 00:22:21.950
It wants to cut us off
so we can't call for help.

00:22:22.169 --> 00:22:26.284
You mean someone --Some nut job
out there just stole all our gear.

00:22:26.367 --> 00:22:29.730
I need to speak with you... in private.

00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:41.151
Okay, let me see dad's journal.

00:22:46.978 --> 00:22:47.854
All right.

00:22:48.730 --> 00:22:49.794
Check that out.

00:22:50.921 --> 00:22:52.188
Oh, come on.

00:22:52.459 --> 00:22:56.363
Windigos are in the Minnesota woods or Northern
Michigan. I've never even heard of one this far west.

00:22:56.264 --> 00:23:02.364
Think about it, Dean -The claws,
the way it can mimic a human voice.

00:23:02.724 --> 00:23:03.710
Great.

00:23:04.367 --> 00:23:06.370
Well, then this is useless.

00:23:11.063 --> 00:23:13.269
We got to get these people to safety.

00:23:15.345 --> 00:23:18.130
All right, listen up. It's time to go.

00:23:18.412 --> 00:23:21.963
Things have gotten more complicated.

00:23:22.594 --> 00:23:22.985
What?

00:23:23.079 --> 00:23:25.598
Whatever's out there,
I think I can handle it.

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:30.213
If you shoot this thing, you're just
gonna make it mad. We have to leave now.

00:23:30.244 --> 00:23:33.226
One, you're talking nonsense, two, you're
in no position to give anybody orders.

00:23:33.227 --> 00:23:34.427
Relax.

00:23:34.582 --> 00:23:37.148
We never should have let you come
out in the first place, all right?

00:23:37.227 --> 00:23:38.228
I'm trying to protect you.

00:23:38.306 --> 00:23:39.401
You protect me?

00:23:39.547 --> 00:23:41.751
I was hunting these woods when your
mommy was still kissing you good night.

00:23:41.752 --> 00:23:42.552
Yeah.

00:23:42.645 --> 00:23:45.398
It's a
damn-Near-Perfect hunter.

00:23:45.899 --> 00:23:47.620
It's smarter than you.

00:23:48.094 --> 00:23:53.492
And it's gonna hunt you down and eat you alive
unless we get your stupid sorry ass out of here.

00:23:53.523 --> 00:23:55.479
You know you're crazy, right? Yeah?

00:23:55.651 --> 00:23:58.268
You ever hunt -Chill out.

00:23:58.331 --> 00:24:02.508
Stop! Stop it. Everybody just stop.

00:24:03.295 --> 00:24:04.140
Look.

00:24:04.390 --> 00:24:06.847
Tommy might still be alive.

00:24:07.347 --> 00:24:09.913
And I'm not leaving here without him.

00:24:14.379 --> 00:24:16.491
It's getting late.

00:24:17.602 --> 00:24:20.027
This thing is a good hunter in the day,

00:24:20.637 --> 00:24:23.000
But an unbelievable hunter at night.

00:24:23.474 --> 00:24:25.758
We'll never beat it
--Not in the dark.

00:24:27.807 --> 00:24:30.154
We need to settle
inand protect ourselves.

00:24:31.140 --> 00:24:32.908
How?

00:24:42.407 --> 00:24:45.630
One more time.That's...?
Anasazi symbols.

00:24:45.786 --> 00:24:49.525
It's for protection. The
windigo can't cross over them.

00:24:50.453 --> 00:24:52.940
Nobody likes a skeptic, Roy.

00:25:03.354 --> 00:25:06.483
You want to tell me what's going
on in that freaky head of yours?

00:25:08.215 --> 00:25:10.296
Dean... No, you're not fine.

00:25:10.984 --> 00:25:13.503
You're like a powder keg,
man. It's not like you.

00:25:14.176 --> 00:25:16.867
I'm supposed to be the
belligerent one, remember?

00:25:20.881 --> 00:25:22.618
Dad's not here.

00:25:25.012 --> 00:25:30.555
I mean, that much we know for sure, right? He
would have left us a message, a sign, right?

00:25:31.447 --> 00:25:33.262
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:25:34.565 --> 00:25:37.381
To tell you the truth, I don't
think dad's ever been to Lost Creek.

00:25:39.211 --> 00:25:42.497
Then let's get these people back
to town, and let's hit the road...

00:25:42.768 --> 00:25:46.507
Go find dad. I mean, why
are we still even here?

00:25:55.175 --> 00:25:56.676
This is why...

00:25:57.099 --> 00:25:58.961
This book.

00:25:59.399 --> 00:26:04.692
This is dad's single most valuable possession.
Everything he knows about every evil thing is in here.

00:26:04.786 --> 00:26:07.070
And he's passed it on to us.

00:26:07.873 --> 00:26:10.689
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:26:11.675 --> 00:26:14.538
You know, saving
people, hunting things...

00:26:14.804 --> 00:26:17.057
The family business.

00:26:19.617 --> 00:26:21.072
That makes no sense.

00:26:21.229 --> 00:26:28.410
Why-Why doesn't he just call us? Why doesn't
he tell us what he wants, tell us where he is?

00:26:29.694 --> 00:26:31.321
I don't know.

00:26:33.011 --> 00:26:34.560
But the way I see it,

00:26:35.921 --> 00:26:39.144
Dad's given us a job to
do, and I intend to do it.

00:26:39.504 --> 00:26:40.834
Dean...

00:26:41.569 --> 00:26:42.461
No.

00:26:43.603 --> 00:26:45.214
I gotta find dad.

00:26:46.028 --> 00:26:48.031
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:26:53.953 --> 00:26:59.210
It's the only thing I can think about. Okay.
All right. Sam, we'll find them. I promise.

00:27:00.540 --> 00:27:01.718
Listen to me.

00:27:01.890 --> 00:27:04.018
You've got to prepare yourself.

00:27:04.925 --> 00:27:07.116
I mean, this search could take a while.

00:27:07.872 --> 00:27:09.578
And all that anger,

00:27:09.781 --> 00:27:13.364
You can't keep it burning over
the long haul. It's gonna kill you.

00:27:14.370 --> 00:27:16.310
You got to have patience, man.

00:27:18.848 --> 00:27:20.459
How do you do it?

00:27:21.257 --> 00:27:23.494
How does dad do it?

00:27:24.887 --> 00:27:27.202
Well, for one, them.

00:27:27.911 --> 00:27:32.135
I mean, I figure our family's so screwed
to hell, maybe we can help some others.

00:27:32.437 --> 00:27:34.721
It makes things a
little bit more bearable.

00:27:39.831 --> 00:27:41.881
And I'll tell you what else helps...

00:27:44.212 --> 00:27:48.155
Killing as many evil sons
of bitches as I possibly can.

00:27:50.796 --> 00:27:52.392
Help me!

00:27:55.583 --> 00:27:56.897
Please...!

00:28:01.208 --> 00:28:02.538
Help!

00:28:03.883 --> 00:28:05.401
It's trying to draw us out.

00:28:05.679 --> 00:28:07.135
Just stay cool. Stay put.

00:28:07.267 --> 00:28:09.306
Inside the magic circle?

00:28:09.395 --> 00:28:11.131
Help!

00:28:12.622 --> 00:28:14.187
Help me!

00:28:16.612 --> 00:28:18.614
Okay, that's no grizzly.

00:28:24.082 --> 00:28:27.179
It's okay. We'll be
all right. I promise.

00:28:30.688 --> 00:28:32.613
It's here.

00:28:39.142 --> 00:28:40.315
I hit it!

00:28:40.362 --> 00:28:41.395
Roy, no!

00:28:41.926 --> 00:28:43.053
Roy!

00:28:43.663 --> 00:28:45.024
Don't move.

00:28:49.284 --> 00:28:52.162
It's over here. Ugh!

00:28:53.795 --> 00:28:54.827
Roy?!

00:29:21.572 --> 00:29:22.621
I don't...

00:29:23.090 --> 00:29:26.078
I mean, these types of things--
They aren't supposed to be real.

00:29:26.313 --> 00:29:28.018
I wish I could tell you different.

00:29:29.228 --> 00:29:31.277
How do we know it's not
out there watching us?

00:29:31.809 --> 00:29:32.967
We don't.

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:35.569
But we're safe for now.

00:29:36.993 --> 00:29:38.839
How do you know about this stuff?

00:29:41.405 --> 00:29:43.189
It kind of runs in the family.

00:29:48.871 --> 00:29:49.888
Hey.

00:29:50.983 --> 00:29:54.019
So, we've got half a
chance in the daylight.

00:29:54.320 --> 00:29:56.620
And I, for one...

00:29:57.105 --> 00:29:59.593
Want to kill this evil son of a bitch.

00:30:00.474 --> 00:30:02.351
Well, hell, you know I'm in.

00:30:02.763 --> 00:30:05.684
Windigo is a cree indian word.
It means, "evil that devours."

00:30:05.685 --> 00:30:07.285
They're hundreds of years old.

00:30:07.347 --> 00:30:13.625
Each one was once a man, sometimes an indian or
other times a frontiers manor a miner or hunter.

00:30:13.771 --> 00:30:16.931
How's a man turn into one of those
things? Well, it's always the same.

00:30:17.041 --> 00:30:18.449
During some harsh winter,

00:30:18.590 --> 00:30:21.985
A guy finds himself starving,
cut off from supplies or help

00:30:22.225 --> 00:30:26.793
Becomes a cannibal to survive, eating
other members of his tribe or camp.

00:30:26.871 --> 00:30:28.780
Like the donner party.

00:30:29.524 --> 00:30:33.298
Cultures all over the world believe that eating
human flesh gives a person certain abilities--

00:30:33.299 --> 00:30:36.299
Speed, strength, immortality.

00:30:36.383 --> 00:30:37.897
If you eat enough of it,

00:30:38.100 --> 00:30:40.385
Over years, you become this ...

00:30:40.588 --> 00:30:42.966
Less-Than-Human
thing.

00:30:43.129 --> 00:30:45.006
You're always hungry.

00:30:45.100 --> 00:30:48.949
So, if that's true, how
can Tommy still be alive?

00:30:51.124 --> 00:30:53.241
You're not gonna like it. Tell me.

00:30:53.569 --> 00:30:56.964
More than anything, a windigo knows
how to last long winters without food.

00:30:57.047 --> 00:31:00.082
It hibernates for years
at a time. When it's awake,

00:31:00.489 --> 00:31:03.654
It keeps its victims
alive. It stores them

00:31:03.983 --> 00:31:06.329
So it can feed whenever it wants.

00:31:07.456 --> 00:31:12.655
If your brother's alive, it's keeping
him somewhere dark, hidden, and safe

00:31:13.312 --> 00:31:15.158
And we got to track it back there.

00:31:15.299 --> 00:31:17.213
And then how do we stop it?

00:31:17.322 --> 00:31:18.402
Well,

00:31:18.668 --> 00:31:21.734
Guns are useless-So are knives.

00:31:22.756 --> 00:31:24.414
Basically...

00:31:24.821 --> 00:31:27.700
We gotta torch the sucker.

00:31:43.964 --> 00:31:44.981
Dean.

00:31:48.173 --> 00:31:49.299
What is it?

00:32:07.348 --> 00:32:08.615
You know,

00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:13.153
I was thinking that those claw
prints, so clear and distinct

00:32:14.800 --> 00:32:17.178
They were almost too easy to follow.

00:32:43.262 --> 00:32:47.000
You okay? His neck's broken.

00:32:47.736 --> 00:32:50.526
Run, run! Go, go, go, go, go!

00:32:59.696 --> 00:33:02.856
Come on. I got you. I got you.

00:33:12.740 --> 00:33:14.102
Hailey!

00:33:24.114 --> 00:33:25.428
Dean!

00:33:26.935 --> 00:33:30.517
If it keeps its victims
alive, why would it kill Roy?

00:33:30.721 --> 00:33:31.753
Honestly?

00:33:32.129 --> 00:33:35.274
I think because Roy shot
at it, he pissed it off.

00:33:42.883 --> 00:33:44.448
They went this way.

00:33:50.352 --> 00:33:52.495
It's better than bread crumbs.

00:35:34.674 --> 00:35:38.648
Hey, it's okay. It's okay. It's okay.

00:35:51.001 --> 00:35:52.159
Dean.

00:35:54.474 --> 00:35:55.945
You. Wake up.

00:35:56.810 --> 00:35:59.297
Dean. Hey. You okay?

00:36:01.863 --> 00:36:02.958
Yeah.

00:36:03.245 --> 00:36:05.529
Hailey... Hailey.

00:36:05.826 --> 00:36:07.923
Wake up. Wake up.

00:36:09.127 --> 00:36:10.270
Gotcha.

00:36:20.442 --> 00:36:23.431
You sure you're all right?
Yeah, yeah. Where is it?

00:36:23.530 --> 00:36:25.376
It's gone for now.

00:36:46.081 --> 00:36:46.957
Tommy.

00:36:50.477 --> 00:36:51.260
Tommy.

00:36:57.434 --> 00:36:59.030
Cut him down.

00:37:12.591 --> 00:37:14.375
We're gonna get you home.

00:37:15.287 --> 00:37:16.695
Check it out.

00:37:17.513 --> 00:37:20.048
Flare guns. Those will work.

00:37:34.500 --> 00:37:38.678
Looks like someone's home for
supper. We'll never out run it.

00:37:42.730 --> 00:37:45.202
You thinking what I'm
thinking? Yeah, I think so.

00:37:48.633 --> 00:37:51.251
All right, listen to me. Stay with
Sam. He's gonna get you out of here.

00:37:51.252 --> 00:37:52.952
What are you gonna do?

00:37:55.569 --> 00:37:58.244
It's chow time, you freakin' bastard!

00:37:58.573 --> 00:38:02.828
Yeah, that's right! Bring
it on, baby! I taste good!

00:38:10.799 --> 00:38:13.005
All right, come on. Hurry!

00:38:18.272 --> 00:38:19.508
Hey!

00:38:20.729 --> 00:38:22.997
Hey, you want some white meat, bitch?!

00:38:23.185 --> 00:38:24.515
I'm right here!

00:38:40.066 --> 00:38:41.680
Get him out of here. Sam, no.

00:38:41.681 --> 00:38:43.681
Go. Go!

00:38:44.071 --> 00:38:44.712
Go.

00:38:54.128 --> 00:38:55.067
Come on.

00:38:56.458 --> 00:38:57.413
Come on.

00:39:12.571 --> 00:39:13.447
Sam!

00:39:15.439 --> 00:39:18.552
Come on. Hurry, hurry, hurry! Go!

00:39:31.334 --> 00:39:32.836
Get behind me.

00:40:15.915 --> 00:40:18.199
Not bad, huh?

00:40:26.355 --> 00:40:31.643
That's when it circled the campsite. I mean,
this grizzly must have weighed 800, 900 pounds.

00:40:33.494 --> 00:40:36.779
So, really, I don't
know how to thank you.

00:40:39.960 --> 00:40:43.559
Must you cheapen the moment? Yeah!

00:40:44.588 --> 00:40:47.655
You riding with your brother? Yeah.

00:40:49.235 --> 00:40:50.299
Let's go.

00:41:02.375 --> 00:41:04.628
I hope you find your father.

00:41:07.971 --> 00:41:09.457
Thanks, Sam.

00:41:27.159 --> 00:41:29.458
Man, I hate camping.

00:41:29.771 --> 00:41:31.007
Me too.

00:41:34.172 --> 00:41:36.394
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:41:37.317 --> 00:41:39.382
Yeah, I know.

00:41:40.795 --> 00:41:43.017
But in the meantime

00:41:44.769 --> 00:41:46.537
I'm driving.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
